WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.480
[suspenseful music playing]

2
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.160
[officer 1] Police! Get down!
Nobody move! Let me see your hands!

3
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.880
[officer 2] Hands on your head!

4
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.800
- [gunshots]
- [officer 3] Get down. get down!

5
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.760
[officer 1] Automatic weapon!

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.840
- [officer 3] Go. go!
- [officer 1] Hands on your head!

7
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.880
- [officer 1] Target down.
- [officer 2] Stay down!

8
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.680
[woman on comm] <i>Target neutralized.</i>

9
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.320
- [knocking on door]
- [officer 1] Police!

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.720
[officer 2] Police. open up!

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.920
- Police. open up!
- [knocking on door]

12
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.640
[Tanya] Explosive set. Ready.

13
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.800
Three.

14
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.200
Two.

15
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.200
One.

16
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.800
[music ends]

17
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.480
[indistinct chatter]

18
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.920
[Djibril] Nice work. man.

19
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.720
[Valère] "Valère in position!"
I get the go. and boom!

20
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.040
They said there's someone
waiting for you at the gate.

21
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.360
Okay. Uh. Cédric. could you give me
something real to do in the next…

22
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.360
Listen. um. Max.

23
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.200
You're a good teammate. and I mean it.
I'm not bullshitting.

24
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.400
In a couple of weeks
they'll decide what's next for you.

25
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.360
I don't know what that is.
but we both know you're finished here.

26
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.640
My job is to make sure the section works
without you and David. okay?

27
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.560
So why would I want to include you. huh?

28
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.280
But take a break. Go see your visitor.

29
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.680
[helicopter whirring overhead]

30
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.600
[distant buzzing]

31
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.760
[lock beeps]

32
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.600
- [indistinct radio chatter]
- [ominous music playing]

33
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.040
[sighs]

34
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.560
ELITE FORCE

35
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.840
[poignant classical piano music playing]

36
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.480
[music continues]

37
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.920
[music stops]

38
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.120
[answering machine beeps]

39
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.280
<i>Hey. this is Manon's voice mail.</i>
<i>If I didn't pick up…</i>

40
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.600
I told her to leave her phone on.
She didn't leave it on.

41
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.360
I don't know if she's going
straight to school or if she's at Nina's.

42
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.240
Are they taking the bus?
Do they need a drive?

43
00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.640
Let me look after Manon.
Stop worrying and go to work.

44
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.880
It'll give me the chance
to follow my dream

45
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.440
of becoming the world's
most accomplished stay-at-home father.

46
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.560
[chuckles]

47
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.440
Keep in mind. I can work on it
here in Paris. or in Hong Kong. same diff.

48
00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.400
Singapore.

49
00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.400
Hong Kong. Singapore. you decide.

50
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.440
[chuckles]

51
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.360
So. you got this?

52
00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.440
Absolutely. piece of cake.

53
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.520
[tender music playing]

54
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.640
- Take your phone.
- Oh. right.

55
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:11.600
- Your coffee?
- Thanks.

56
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.440
Thanks. you're sweet.

57
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.280
I love you.

58
00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.720
[indistinct radio chatter]

59
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.760
Your father had just joined the force
with David.

60
00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.560
David hadn't met Jess yet.

61
00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.440
We weren't even your age.
We were still kids.

62
00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.360
Laurent was deployed
for four months in New Caledonia.

63
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.680
And because of my job. I couldn't go.

64
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.880
A while after he came back.
I noticed I was late.

65
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.080
I did a test. I was pregnant. with you.

66
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.080
We were overjoyed.

67
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.600
Our parents thought we were too young
but we didn't care.

68
00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.080
The day you were born
was the happiest day of our lives.

69
00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.080
[pensive music playing]

70
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.680
You were growing up

71
00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.600
and we wanted to give you
a little brother. or a little sister.

72
00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.200
We tried again.
For weeks and months. It didn't work.

73
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.480
We went to see a specialist.
and we learned the truth.

74
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.440
Laurent was unable to have children.

75
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.240
Up to then. I'd always thought
Laurent was your father.

76
00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.160
Why are you telling me all this?

77
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.960
So I'll forgive you? Is that it?

78
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.920
So I say. "It's no big deal. Mom"?

79
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.600
I don't need your forgiveness.

80
00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.680
Having you was the best thing
that ever happened to me.

81
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.640
- I won't apologize for that.
- But you lied to me. you…

82
00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.120
You cheated on Dad.

83
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.280
With David?

84
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.400
Why didn't you tell me
the truth after he died?

85
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.000
Would it have helped you to know?

86
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.760
I just wanted to protect you. I…

87
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.160
Of course it would have helped me.
I have a father who's alive!

88
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.840
I had the right to know!

89
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.400
[music turns poignant]

90
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.240
I was the one
who kept David out of your life.

91
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.200
What?

92
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.880
Your father died
because David told him everything.

93
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.800
What right did he have
to see you after that?

94
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.120
Because of that one time. 25 years ago?

95
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.600
You stole my father from me.
don't you understand?

96
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.280
You had no fucking right!

97
00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.760
[breathes shakily]

98
00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.760
[alarm blaring]

99
00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:27.960
[Max] Ah. fuck.

100
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.200
[Nathalie] Max!

101
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.800
Oh. shit…

102
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.200
[cell phone buzzing]

103
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.560
Yeah?

104
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.480
<i>David. it's Valère.</i>
<i>Where's your daughter right now?</i>

105
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.440
What is this?
Why are you asking about my daughter?

106
00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.640
Her music school.

107
00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.760
<i>There's a hostage situation.</i>
<i>but we don't know who's inside.</i>

108
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.920
[suspenseful music playing]

109
00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.120
FRENCH ARMY

110
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.320
[pilot] <i>Airborne on approach.</i>
<i>Target confirmed.</i>

111
00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.600
[officer] Sir. sir. you can't go through.

112
00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.120
[police sirens blaring]

113
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.040
Okay. it's fine.

114
00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.120
[suspenseful music continues]

115
00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.160
[sniper 1] <i>Fox 1 in position.</i>

116
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.040
[sniper 2] <i>Fox 3 in position.</i>

117
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.040
[drone whirring]

118
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.760
[officer] <i>This is Delta 5.</i>
<i>we're at security.</i>

119
00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.720
<i>Entrances have been rigged</i>
<i>with explosives.</i>

120
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.680
<i>Identification in progress.</i>

121
00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.240
[suspenseful music continues]

122
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.040
[pilot] <i>Copy that.</i>

123
00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.120
<i>We're maintaining position</i>
<i>above the target.</i>

124
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.080
[sirens blaring distantly]

125
00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.680
Check if the command post
has a list of hostages. okay?

126
00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.560
- [Chloé] Okay.
- A quick briefing. everyone.

127
00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.720
The van parked out front.
it's been there overnight.

128
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.200
- I'll check it out.
- Sure. go ahead.

129
00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.760
So. listen up.

130
00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.720
They arrived yesterday
and spent the night there.

131
00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.400
They have assault weapons.
They're masked and prepared.

132
00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.040
At 9:00 a.m. they started shooting.

133
00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.600
Two people were wounded.
but they managed to escape.

134
00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.160
Since then.
we've heard nothing from the terrorists.

135
00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.400
We assume they're holed up
inside somewhere.

136
00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.000
We've set up these three fire supports.
All on the roof of the station. okay?

137
00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.680
Have we identified the Oscars?

138
00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.880
- We're expecting that any minute now.
- And where are we on tactical assault?

139
00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.040
Nowhere yet. I have no visibility.

140
00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.200
We have a 55 on the targets?

141
00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.240
Fuck. Are we in contact
with them. at least?

142
00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.480
They're not answering our calls.
They're well-prepared.

143
00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.240
Thanks. David. I know what I'm doing.

144
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.440
Here are my concerns.

145
00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.000
They have hostages.
but they haven't made any demands.

146
00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.880
We don't know what they want.
but we know what we have to do.

147
00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.840
Get your teams together
and be ready to move in. Let's do it.

148
00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.920
[indistinct chatter]

149
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.560
- We're in contact with building security.
- Calling them now.

150
00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:35.680
[Cédric] Okay. come on.
I need that hostage list.

151
00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.240
Hang on. here it is.

152
00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.960
- We're good. we got the list.
- [Cédric] Print it out. please.

153
00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.720
[tense music playing]

154
00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.320
I'm with them now.

155
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.120
We don't know if she's inside yet.

156
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.440
Okay. so what do you know?

157
00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.120
Not a lot. actually.
They still haven't told me much.

158
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.560
<i>But of course. as soon as I get something.</i>
<i>I'll let you know.</i>

159
00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.000
Okay. Maybe I should try Nina again.
I can't reach her either.

160
00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.360
- Hold on.
- What is it?

161
00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.000
[music darkens]

162
00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.400
She's in there.

163
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.720
Huh?

164
00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.800
[breathes shakily]

165
00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:22.520
[gasps]

166
00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.040
[breathes shakily]

167
00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.880
[sobs]

168
00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.720
She's my baby.

169
00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.240
Jess.

170
00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.320
{\an8}[Jess sobbing]

171
00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.600
Jess. I'm gonna get her out.

172
00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.680
I promise. You hear me?

173
00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.920
[crying]

174
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.120
<i>I promise you.</i>

175
00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.080
Call you back.

176
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.600
No. no. no. no. wait. wait!

177
00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.280
- [crying]
- [call ends]

178
00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:51.880
[phone clatters]

179
00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.440
David!

180
00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.160
David!

181
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.960
What are you doing?
Thinking of going in alone?

182
00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.760
Leave this to us.
We know what we're doing.

183
00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:05.960
Oh. yeah?

184
00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.040
Why haven't you formed
a tactical column already?

185
00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.160
[Cédric] We don't know
how many terrorists there are.

186
00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.680
They've rigged doors.
We don't know where to send in a column.

187
00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.320
I didn't say send in a column.
I said you should form one!

188
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.080
If you send in a column at the last second
and you haven't formed one.

189
00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.000
you lost 30 seconds.

190
00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.440
We don't even know where they are!

191
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.320
We have no videos.
nobody's talked to them.

192
00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.560
We have no clue what they want.
We're not ready.

193
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.640
Hey! I'm not an idiot. Manon's in there.
but you're not running things.

194
00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.800
That's my job. okay?
You have to let me do it.

195
00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.600
Oh. that's fine. You've made it
very clear that you're in command.

196
00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:35.520
Here's what we'll do.

197
00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.560
You worry about your team.
I'll worry about myself.

198
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:41.000
Cool it. Calm down. There's no fucking way
I'm letting you in there and you know it.

199
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.520
- Get the fuck off me!
- [dark music playing]

200
00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:49.840
[man whistles]

201
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:56.800
I'm sorry.

202
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.200
I'm sorry. Cédric.

203
00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.160
You're emotional.

204
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.360
It's normal. but it's messing you up.

205
00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:08.840
You're gonna have to trust me. okay?
Look at me.

206
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.400
We'll get every last hostage out of there.
safe and sound.

207
00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:14.720
Okay?

208
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.520
- Yeah.
- If you're working with us. focus.

209
00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.960
You're the one who knows the layout.
Can you focus? Can you keep it together?

210
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.120
I'm good.

211
00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.520
I'm good.

212
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.680
So. let's go.

213
00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.760
[music fades]

214
00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.480
Get back to work. Show time's over. guys.

215
00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.840
{\an8}Witnesses report that several men.
all masked and heavily armed.

216
00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.520
{\an8}burst into the conservatory
at around 9:00 this morning

217
00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.920
and took students hostage.

218
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.120
Police are already on the scene.

219
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.200
{\an8}We have no further information yet
about what is clearly a major operation.

220
00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.520
[man] We're waiting to hear
whether authorities set up

221
00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.880
a direct line of communication
with the hostage takers

222
00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.360
in order to begin negotiations.

223
00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.440
So far the hostage takers
remain a mystery.

224
00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.760
We don't know the group's name
or what they are demanding.

225
00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.840
[indistinct chatter]

226
00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.120
We have a chopper
hovering in this location.

227
00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.360
but it can't stay there long.

228
00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.920
We have to move fast.
I also sent out a drone.

229
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.640
We know that every entrance
is rigged with explosives.

230
00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.280
With all these windows.
they can see us coming. Except here.

231
00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.640
There's a blind spot in this building.

232
00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:12.560
You see all the green here?
Those are telecommunications cables.

233
00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:16.320
If we plug into them. we'll be able
to use all the security cameras.

234
00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.880
- Is that the rest of the network?
- Yeah.

235
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.280
This is where we plug in.
which means we put the column here.

236
00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.080
Valère. take whoever you need
from section 1.

237
00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.560
Set up a tactical column there.

238
00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.640
Okay. Can I have one of your guys
to hook me up to the cameras?

239
00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.760
Yeah. sure. Uh. Rapha?

240
00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:31.520
- Can you go with Valère?
- No problem.

241
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.200
- [Chloé] Take whatever gear you need.
- Okay.

242
00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.960
[Chloé] I'll go back to tracking the van.

243
00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:39.040
[indistinct chatter]

244
00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.120
Cédric gave me the okay
to take part in the mission.

245
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.760
I'm really sorry about Manon.

246
00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.680
She's my little sister.

247
00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:02.280
We'll get her out of there. Don't worry.

248
00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.520
Stay strong.

249
00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.360
[poignant music playing]

250
00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.040
[cell phone buzzing]

251
00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:13.640
Yeah? Yeah. I'm coming. I'm on my way.

252
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.200
I'm not leaving. officer.

253
00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.320
I've told you three times now.
You have to back up.

254
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.400
She's with me.

255
00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.680
She's with me!

256
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.680
Okay.

257
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.360
Open up. Let her through. guys.

258
00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.880
[dramatic music playing]

259
00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.480
[Valère] Right. focus up.

260
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.480
Lock in. guys.

261
00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:50.360
[dramatic music continues]

262
00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.240
Move out.

263
00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:09.520
[music fades]

264
00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.320
My girl's here. so I'm here.

265
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.800
Jess. will you stay in the car?

266
00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.080
Okay.

267
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.160
I'll be back.

268
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.640
With Manon.

269
00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:23.800
I know.

270
00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.560
[indistinct chatter]

271
00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.720
[police siren blares in distance]

272
00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.000
- [officer 1] Do you see the hostages?
- [officer 2] Negative. I do not.

273
00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.880
[sighs]

274
00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.080
[woman on radio] <i>Family members</i>
<i>are just starting to arrive on the scene.</i>

275
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.600
<i>where a crisis team has been set up</i>
<i>to provide psychological support.</i>

276
00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.520
<i>Clearly. the families are feeling shock…</i>

277
00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.120
[tense music playing]

278
00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:00.360
[Valère] We just entered at door 3.

279
00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.760
50 yards to the lobby.

280
00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.840
[tense music continues]

281
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:12.440
[indistinct radio chatter]

282
00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.440
How's it going. Cédric?

283
00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.280
[Cédric] Should have access soon.
Pull up the images.

284
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:18.480
Valère?

285
00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.440
- What's your status?
- [Valère] <i>Entering the lobby.</i>

286
00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.520
[suspenseful music playing]

287
00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.680
[Max] Backup in position.

288
00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.760
[suspenseful music continues]

289
00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.440
[Valère] We're in position.

290
00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.280
- Okay.
- We're good.

291
00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.000
[Rapha] Connecting.

292
00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:27.680
[beeps]

293
00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.280
- [Rapha] <i>Link established.</i>
<i>- </i>We're in.

294
00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.560
Oscars and Tangos in the auditorium.
Three armed Tangos. Nine Oscars in hoods.

295
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.160
- Hostages bunched together.
- [Chloé] Check the other camera feeds.

296
00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:41.840
- [gunshot]
- [grunts]

297
00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:43.840
- [Valère] We're taking fire!
- [groans]

298
00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.760
- [grunts and groans]
- [Max] Rapha!

299
00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.320
[Valère] Two officers down.
I repeat. we have two officers down!

300
00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.040
Valère. take cover! Everyone out of there!
Pull back. pull back!

301
00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.560
- [Chloé] Shots fired!
- [Rapha groans]

302
00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:53.920
[Valère] We got you. Rapha. okay?

303
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.440
[intense music playing]

304
00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.840
[grunting]

305
00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:03.920
- [gunshot]
- [screams]

306
00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.600
[Cédric] We have shots fired!

307
00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.040
[Max] You okay?
Are you okay? Can you hear me?

308
00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.360
[David] It's gotta be
from the building next door. Cédric!

309
00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.400
[Valère] <i>We're evacuating.</i>
<i>we're evacuating.</i>

310
00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:15.320
Go on.

311
00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.640
Schwepps. two pairs with me!

312
00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:20.600
Valère. do you read me?

313
00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:25.160
- [Max] Come on! Move!
- [Valère] You can make it! Keep going!

314
00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.200
- [Valère] <i>We're evacuating two wounded.</i>
<i>- </i>Fuck!

315
00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.880
[intense music continues]

316
00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.960
[officer on comm] <i>Confirmed.</i>
<i>we have shots fired next door.</i>

317
00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:46.920
[heavy gunfire]

318
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.200
[David] We're taking heavy fire
at the east entrance.

319
00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.320
[screams]

320
00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.160
[gunfire]

321
00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:54.440
- [officer 1] Go. go. go!
- [officer 2] Move it!

322
00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.240
[people screaming]

323
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.440
David. report position. Do you have cover?

324
00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:00.160
- [David] <i>We're in.</i>
- Wait.

325
00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.840
[Cédric] Secure your position.
I'm sending back up to you now.

326
00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.760
- [indistinct shouting]
- [officer] Go. go!

327
00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:06.320
[sirens blaring]

328
00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:09.480
[Cédric] <i>Reposition. north-west entrance.</i>
<i>Repeat. north-west.</i>

329
00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.320
[man on radio]
<i>We just heard isolated gunshots</i>

330
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.840
<i>followed by bursts of automatic fire.</i>

331
00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.400
<i>This could indicate that GIGN</i>
<i>is entering the building.</i>

332
00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:18.000
[suspenseful music playing]

333
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.880
- [man 1] GSW! Clear the way!
- [woman 1] I've got a crash cart!

334
00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.040
[indistinct chatter]

335
00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.480
[man 1] Support his pelvis. His pelvis.
They're loading them now.

336
00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.280
- [woman 1] One. two. three.
- [man 1] Get him on the gurney.

337
00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.440
- Okay. strap her in.
- [woman 1] Need oxygen!

338
00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.160
[man 1] You're taking the second victim.

339
00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:39.200
- [woman 1] Move out of the way.
- [man 1] You're gonna be fine.

340
00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.440
[officer] If you need backup.
let me know right away.

341
00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.960
[man 1] You good?

342
00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:45.720
- Fine. that's it.
- [Max] We need you. Okay? You'll be fine.

343
00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:47.360
Keep your eyes open. you'll be okay.

344
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:50.200
- [man 1] Let me know.
- [man 2] She was shot on the right side.

345
00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.640
- [man 3] You'll be fine. Rapha.
- [woman 1] Come on!

346
00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.160
[woman 2] Can you hear me. ma'am?

347
00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.840
- [man 1] Give me the gauze pads.
- [man 2] Gauze.

348
00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:03.200
Open your eyes. ma'am.
Squeeze my hand.

349
00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.040
Ma'am. open your eyes.

350
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.440
Open your eyes if you can hear me.

351
00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.560
- [man 2] Careful.
- [woman 2] Keep pressure.

352
00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:12.360
You're with the paramedics.
Stay with us now. ma'am.

353
00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.360
- [man 2] Eyes open.
- [woman 2] Open your eyes.

354
00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:15.560
[woman 3] Open the gates.

355
00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:17.600
[man 3] Moving in. let's go!

356
00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.680
[intense music playing]

357
00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.840
- [officer 1] Clear!
- [officer 2] Clear!

358
00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:24.480
[David] Go!

359
00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.800
Wait. Schwepps. Hang on. stop.

360
00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.960
We're going up on the roof.

361
00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.240
[man on radio] <i>We're getting reports</i>
<i>that GIGN officers</i>

362
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.200
<i>have been injured in an exchange</i>
<i>of gunfire in the building.</i>

363
00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.440
[officer] Chloé. look at this camera feed.

364
00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.200
We've got two more at the top.

365
00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:09.160
[Chloé] Cédric. there's a total
of five Tangos in the auditorium.

366
00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:14.000
There it is! I've got the van on a camera.

367
00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:18.080
- It was at a self-storage yesterday.
- Okay. we're on it.

368
00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.200
Rico. come here. take over for me.

369
00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.520
[tense music playing]

370
00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:38.280
[hostages whimpering]

371
00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.320
Shut the fuck up!

372
00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.480
[breathing heavily]

373
00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:46.800
Cédric.

374
00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:51.040
Terrorist's on the line.
She wants to talk to David.

375
00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.720
- David?
- [David] <i>Yeah. go ahead.</i>

376
00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.840
[Cédric] <i>Terrorist on the line.</i>
<i>It's a woman.</i>

377
00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.520
<i>Chloé and I are listening in.</i>

378
00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:02.320
She wants to talk to you.

379
00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:05.920
[David] Okay. put her on.

380
00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.640
- [Cédric] <i>Connecting.</i>
- [line chimes]

381
00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.960
[Amal exhales slowly]

382
00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.640
[static crackles]

383
00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.720
[ominous music playing]

384
00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.400
[Amal exhales slowly]

385
00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.640
Surely you must know this is personal.

386
00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.640
<i>The GIGN took everything from me.</i>

387
00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:42.080
<i>France took everything from me.</i>

388
00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:45.920
But you took my whole family.

389
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:49.480
<i>My girl. my husband. my blood.</i>

390
00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.560
- I'll find your girl. I have a daughter.
- Save her.

391
00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:55.560
Amal Mayard?

392
00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.400
- [Amal] <i>Commander Berger.</i>
- Oh. shit.

393
00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:06.280
[Amal] <i>Like I said.</i>
<i>it's personal between you and me.</i>

394
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.560
LAST FLOOR - FREIGHT ELEVATOR

395
00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.480
I'm not here to negotiate. David.

396
00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.880
I'm here today
to take everything from you.

397
00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.760
And the whole world will be watching.

398
00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:20.720
[closes phone]

399
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.800
[music darkens]

400
00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:26.560
Oh. fuck.

401
00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.880
{\an8}In the army she specialized

402
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.760
<i>in long-range shooting.</i>

403
00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.320
I'll take care of Amal.

404
00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:35.960
Let's go. guys.

405
00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:37.800
[Cédric] <i>Tango leader</i>
<i>is on a suicide mission.</i>

406
00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:40.080
She's gonna execute the hostages.
We have to move in now.

407
00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.920
- [police sirens blaring]
- [suspenseful music playing]

408
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:48.760
- [Valère] It's nothing.
- Lemme see your arm.

409
00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.920
- Nothing to see.
- I have to check. It's my job.

410
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:53.440
See? It's nothing. It's just bullshit.

411
00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:55.280
- Is he fit?
- Damn right I'm fit.

412
00:22:55.360 --> 00:22:57.240
- [Cédric] Great. everyone in the Sherpa.
- Nice.

413
00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:03.320
[suspenseful music playing]

414
00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:07.680
- [elevator chimes]
- [doors open]

415
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.720
Guys! Guys! Listen up for a minute.

416
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.920
We're going into a building full of CL-20.

417
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.960
No matter what. we can't let them
detonate those explosives.

418
00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:33.200
As you know. our motto is.
"A commitment to life. to all lives."

419
00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:36.080
Unfortunately. there are situations
that call for hard choices.

420
00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:40.480
So. Valère. Djibril. PJ. Nico. Max.
I'm going to need your sniper skills.

421
00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:42.960
If we want to save the hostages.
we have to do some shooting.

422
00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:45.960
It's the only way.
But you're only gonna get one shot.

423
00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:47.720
So you better make sure it counts.

424
00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:50.080
This is an operation
of the utmost delicacy.

425
00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:52.920
Let's do a good job
so we all go home tonight. please.

426
00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.920
- Alright. let's go! In the truck!
- [lively chatter]

427
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.520
- Gonna be okay. Valère?
- Totally.

428
00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:58.800
- You got this. Demo?
- Hell yeah.

429
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.920
- [Cédric] Deal with the CL-20.
- All set to move. I'm sticking with Recon.

430
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.880
[Valère] Okay. guys. let's go.

431
00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:06.520
- [tense music playing]
- [elevator chimes]

432
00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:23.760
[Chloé] <i>Yeah?</i>

433
00:24:23.840 --> 00:24:27.440
Chloé. on the cams for the music school.
can you see the targets go in?

434
00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:30.440
[Chloé] Affirmative.

435
00:24:30.520 --> 00:24:32.560
[David] <i>And can you see them coming out?</i>

436
00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:37.040
Uh. negative.

437
00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:38.360
Ah. fuck.

438
00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:41.320
Somehow. they still fired at us
from the building next door.

439
00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:42.840
so there has to be. uh…

440
00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:44.400
[Chloé] <i>An accomplice. maybe?</i>

441
00:24:44.480 --> 00:24:45.920
An underground passage.

442
00:24:47.400 --> 00:24:49.040
Cédric. I'm dividing the team.

443
00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:52.000
Okay. guys. let's switch up the plan.

444
00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:54.040
We're looking for a tunnel. Schwepps.

445
00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:56.360
You two go down that hallway.
We'll meet at the end.

446
00:24:56.440 --> 00:24:59.240
Sergio. you guys take the third floor.

447
00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:00.520
We'll meet at the end.

448
00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:03.600
[Chloé] <i>Okay. I'm 15 minutes out.</i>
<i>I'll call you from the warehouse.</i>

449
00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:05.720
[Cédric] <i>Copy that. Sending in the Sherpa.</i>

450
00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:08.560
[indistinct radio chatter]

451
00:25:09.880 --> 00:25:11.080
[Max] Cédric?

452
00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.600
Any news about Rapha?

453
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.760
She's in good hands.
Keep your head in the game. Max.

454
00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:16.720
You know how it works.

455
00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:19.080
If a teammate goes down.
step over them and keep moving.

456
00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:21.120
If you can't handle it.
get off the truck now.

457
00:25:22.840 --> 00:25:24.440
[Sherpa engine starts]

458
00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:30.480
[dramatic music playing]

459
00:26:07.960 --> 00:26:10.760
[music intensifies]

460
00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:51.880
- [glass shatters]
- [music fades]

461
00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:57.080
[tense music playing]

462
00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:07.360
[Cédric] <i>We just entered building B.</i>

463
00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:10.560
There's a man down in hallway S.

464
00:27:12.760 --> 00:27:16.160
[Sergio] <i>Team 1 proceeding</i>
<i>through hallway V. Nothing to report.</i>

465
00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:20.200
[Schwepps] <i>Team 2 NSTR in hallway D.</i>

466
00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.360
[Cédric] <i>We're crossing over</i>
<i>to building A.</i>

467
00:27:27.440 --> 00:27:29.960
[tense music continues]

468
00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:33.800
Delta Echo Alpha Delta.

469
00:27:39.960 --> 00:27:41.640
[Cédric] Separate columns.

470
00:28:03.240 --> 00:28:04.320
Stop there!

471
00:28:04.400 --> 00:28:06.880
[tense music continues]

472
00:28:06.960 --> 00:28:08.560
Turn around nice and slow.

473
00:28:10.440 --> 00:28:11.960
Put your weapon on the ground.

474
00:28:15.120 --> 00:28:16.480
Hands on your head.

475
00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:19.120
- [grunting]
- [groans]

476
00:28:19.200 --> 00:28:20.360
[grunts]

477
00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:22.880
[groans]

478
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.960
No!

479
00:28:31.760 --> 00:28:32.920
That's not the plan.

480
00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:34.520
[David groans]

481
00:28:38.600 --> 00:28:39.520
